<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="022" project="spaarke-notification-spine-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Kind-Generic Pending/Poll Fallback Endpoint (ADR-032 Degrade Path)</title>
    <phase>2 Layer C + communication-arrived</phase>
    <gate>blocked-until:012</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>New unconditional BFF endpoint over the outbox; forms the platform-wide ADR-032 degrade path every host shares — meets root CLAUDE.md §8 FULL criteria (bff-api tag, new endpoint).</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Straightforward read endpoint over an already-built outbox service (task 012) — no architectural judgment required.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>Q</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>012</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, api</tags>
    <estimated-effort>3h</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Add a kind-generic pending/poll endpoint over the task-012 outbox so every host (workspace, PCF, code page) has ONE degrade path when SignalR is off or unreachable, and so a client that missed a live ping still gets the signal on next load or next poll tick.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. Deep experience with ASP.NET Core Minimal APIs and ADR-032 degrade-path design.</role>

  <goal>An authenticated GET /api/notifications/pending endpoint returns the calling user's pending outbox rows (kind-generic — every active kind in the same response shape) sourced from task 012's outbox read API. The endpoint behaves IDENTICALLY regardless of SignalR state — it IS the degrade path, not a SignalR-aware branch — so with the SignalR delivery service (task 020) disabled or absent, a written outbox row is still retrievable through this endpoint.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Spec FR-06 + NFR-04. This is the ADR-032 degrade path every consumer shares: task 021's client library falls back to it on disconnect; task 025's contract-lock note cites it as R3's polling-only path. It is deliberately kind-generic (unlike the existing appnotification-only useBriefingNotifications hook) because multiple active kinds (suggestion, communication-assessed, communication-arrived) must all surface through the same fallback mechanism.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Notifications/</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/CommunicationEndpoints.cs</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.DailyBriefing.Components/src/hooks/useBriefingNotifications.ts</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-032-bff-nullobject-kill-switch.md</file>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">The endpoint reads from task 012's outbox service's read API — it does NOT re-implement outbox querying and does NOT read appnotification. It is a NEW store (the outbox), not a reformatting of the existing useBriefingNotifications appnotification-only path.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-032">The endpoint is registered UNCONDITIONALLY and its behavior does NOT branch on whether SignalR is enabled — it always serves whatever is currently pending in the outbox for the caller. Its correctness under "SignalR off" is a consequence of being SignalR-agnostic, not a special-cased fallback branch.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">The endpoint derives the caller's identity server-side from the validated JWT (oid) — it MUST NOT accept a target userId query/body parameter (no cross-user pending reads).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Response items carry the same envelope shape as task 013's contract (IDs + minimal display metadata only) — no message bodies, no privileged content, no pre-authorized action tokens (NFR-02/03).</constraint>
    <constraint source="bff-extensions.md §C">Minimal API only, mapped via a Map{Feature}Endpoints extension, .RequireAuthorization(), Results.Problem(...) for errors.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-032-bff-nullobject-kill-switch.md</file>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="minimal-api-endpoint-group" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/CommunicationEndpoints.cs">MapGroup + RequireAuthorization + WithName/WithDescription/Produces&lt;T&gt; — copy this shape.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <justification>
    <existing>useBriefingNotifications (src/client/shared/Spaarke.DailyBriefing.Components/src/hooks/useBriefingNotifications.ts) reads appnotification only — no kind discriminator, no outbox awareness.</existing>
    <extension>No — different store (the new outbox, not appnotification) and a kind-generic contract useBriefingNotifications was never designed for; extending it would conflate two stores.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>No degrade path when SignalR is off (NFR-04 fails outright); R3's polling fallback (their task 045, per the contract-lock note already drafted at their side) has no target endpoint to poll.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Read task 012's outbox service's actual read/query API (method signatures, filter-by-user, kind field) — do not assume its shape.</step>
    <step order="2">Add GET /api/notifications/pending to a Map{Feature}Endpoints extension (reuse or extend task 020's NotificationsEndpoints.cs if it exists, or create Api/Notifications/NotificationsEndpoints.cs), authenticated, deriving caller identity from the JWT.</step>
    <step order="3">Return the caller's pending outbox rows in envelope shape (task 013 types) — kind-generic, no filtering by kind unless the client requests it via an optional query parameter.</step>
    <step order="4">Register the endpoint mapping UNCONDITIONALLY; verify no asymmetric registration against task 012's outbox service (bff-extensions.md §F.1 static-scan recipe).</step>
    <step order="5">Write the degrade seam test under tests/integration/seam/Notifications/: with the SignalR delivery service's null-object active (SignalR "off"), a producer writes an outbox row, then a request to GET /api/notifications/pending returns that row.</step>
    <step order="6">Update tasks/TASK-INDEX.md: set task 022 to ✅ completed.</step>
    <step order="7">Document any deviations in projects/spaarke-notification-spine-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If task 012's outbox read API cannot filter/scope rows to the calling user without an app-only cross-user query, STOP and escalate before adding a workaround — cross-user leakage in a "pending" endpoint is the same class of compliance risk as task 023's fan-out leak.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build/test .NET</tool>
    <tool name="terminal">Shell</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Notifications/NotificationsEndpoints.cs (pending handler, added to or alongside task 020's file)</output>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/seam/Notifications/PendingPollFallbackSeamTests.cs</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given SignalR is disabled (null-object registered, per task 020), when a producer writes an outbox row for user U and then user U calls GET /api/notifications/pending, then the response includes that row.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given SignalR is enabled and a client already received a live ping for a row, when the same client subsequently calls GET /api/notifications/pending before dismissing it, then the row still appears (idempotent read; dismissal is a separate operation owned by task 012's outbox service, not by this endpoint).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given user A calls GET /api/notifications/pending, when the response is inspected, then it contains ONLY user A's pending rows — no row belonging to another user, regardless of any query parameter supplied.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given an unauthenticated request to GET /api/notifications/pending, when it is sent, then the endpoint returns 401.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the outbox contains rows of multiple kinds (suggestion, communication-assessed, communication-arrived) for the same user, when GET /api/notifications/pending is called without a kind filter, then all active-kind rows are returned in the same response shape.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a response item is inspected against task 013's envelope contract, when compared, then it carries IDs + minimal display metadata only — no message body, no privileged content, no pre-authorized action token.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A tests/integration/seam/Notifications/** test exists proving the SignalR-off → written row → retrievable-via-endpoint degrade path (NFR-04) as an executable seam test.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>This endpoint is the SAME degrade path both R3's polling-only hosts and this project's own client library (task 021) consume — do not design it as a SpaarkeAi-specific or comms-specific shape.

  COMPLETION SUMMARY (2026-07-21): Implemented `GET /api/notifications/pending` on the existing
  task-020 `NotificationsEndpoints.cs` MapGroup — kind-generic, SignalR-agnostic (no SignalR
  dependency in the handler signature at all). Caller identity derived server-side from the JWT
  `oid` claim (mirrors `NegotiateAsync`), resolved to a Dataverse `systemuserid` via
  `ISystemUserIdentityResolver.ResolveSystemUserIdAsync`; a null resolution returns 200 + empty
  list (not an error). Rows come from `OutboxService.GetPendingAsync(systemUserId)`, projected to
  `{ outboxRowId, kind, envelope }` where `envelope` is the task-013 envelope JSON parsed to a raw
  `JsonElement` (kind-generic — no per-kind switch). Optional `?kind=` query filter reuses
  `NotificationKind`'s existing wire converter; unrecognized values return 400. No DI changes — both
  dependencies were already registered. Seam test
  `tests/integration/seam/Notifications/PendingPollFallbackSeamTests.cs` (6 tests, all passing)
  covers: SignalR-off degrade path, cross-user isolation (2 tests), multi-kind + filter, invalid
  filter 400, and the REAL `SystemUserIdentityResolver` production class (Dataverse boundary
  mocked). Deviation: the handler was marked `internal` (not `private`) specifically so the seam
  test can call it directly per the established `InternalsVisibleTo` seam convention in this
  category, avoiding a full `WebApplicationFactory` host for a service composed of two already-unit-
  tested collaborators. `dotnet build` 0 errors; `dotnet test` (Notifications scope) 75/75 passed.
  No new package — publish-size delta ~0, no re-publish run.</notes>

